# What must never reach the production image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked
# into a layer — and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# docker-compose supplies these at runtime through `env_file`. Copying them in
# as well would publish the signing key with the image, and a leaked
# DIFAAC_SECRET_KEY forges any session token it likes.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- The pre-migration database --------------------------------------------
# app/difaac.db still holds every user's bcrypt hash. The application has not
# read it since the move to PostgreSQL; it exists only as the source for the
# one-off migration, and it belongs on the developer's machine, not in a
# published artefact.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Build noise -----------------------------------------------------------
# The virtualenv is built for the developer's OS and would shadow the wheels
# the image installs for Linux.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Not needed to serve requests ------------------------------------------
tests/
scripts/
*.md
*.log
